OL,3,GNEWSACommunity garden's food supply hit
OL,4,Aby dry summer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA community garden has been forced to
OL,7,Fthrow away food which was destined for
OL,8,Fthe local community as a result of
OL,9,Frecent dry weather.
OL,11,FVolunteers from Northern Lily Community
OL,12,FHub in Oldham said up to three quarters
OL,13,Fof its plants, fruit and vegetables
OL,14,Fsimply did not survive the hot summer.
OL,16,F"Normally we grow over a tonne of food
OL,17,Fwhich equates to 12,700 meals worth and
OL,18,Fwe give that away to our community,"
OL,19,FVictoria Holden from the garden said.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,409,400,260,160,0,100
